    {
      "id": "TEST-EXEC-020",
      "name": "MALFORMED_EMAIL_REJECTED",
      "note": "MALFORMED_EMAIL_REJECTED: a structurally invalid but non-empty address ('test [at] example.com') is now NOT_READY at the queue layer and never reaches the payload builder, so no payload.to/payload.email is staged and no Outreach Log row can claim EXECUTION_SUCCEEDED for an undeliverable address. readinessFor applies isWellFormedEmail (EMAIL_RE) on the explicit email channel; validatePayload applies the same check as defense-in-depth for any path that reaches the execution boundary with a malformed address. The result card is still present and still counts as executed_skipped=1: the engine emits a SKIPPED card for every queue item, so the fix is visible in ready_candidates (1 -> 0) and in the card's reason (DRY_RUN -> NOT_READY) rather than in a disappearing card.",
      "run": {
        "mode": "DRY_RUN",
        "provider": "NOT_CONFIGURED"
      },
      "message_variants": {
        "TEST-EXEC-020": "cold-outreach-v1"
      },
